{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 10, :comments ["<b>The roaring of the lion</b> — R. Moses haKohen, of blessed memory, explained it: the roaring of the lion, and the meaning is that HaShem sets lions and beasts against them. And R. Jonah explained נתעו as נלתעו, from מלתעות (fangs). And both are far-fetched, and its meaning: that the roar of Elohim is likened to the roaring of a lion over its prey." "And he explained נתעו — like יתעו, so as not to eat." "And the word נתעו — refers back to the young lions, and its meaning is like: הנה זה בא."], :book :job, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 4, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Job -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/eyov/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:01:44.339815336Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}